WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.554
Context selection is the act of choosing what the model actually needs for the task.

00:00:05.554 --> 00:00:08.067
More information is not always better.

00:00:08.067 --> 00:00:12.431
Start by identifying the decision, question, or artifact you want.

00:00:12.431 --> 00:00:16.332
Then include the source material that directly supports it.

00:00:16.332 --> 00:00:22.151
Remove duplicates, stale drafts, irrelevant examples, and material that only adds noise.

00:00:22.151 --> 00:00:26.515
Selection is often more valuable than simply expanding the prompt.

00:00:26.515 --> 00:00:30.879
Compression means reducing material while preserving what matters.

00:00:30.879 --> 00:00:39.608
A useful summary can keep key facts, decisions, assumptions, constraints, evidence, and open questions while leaving out repetition.

00:00:39.608 --> 00:00:43.840
Conversation history often benefits from periodic summarization.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:51.774
Long documents may benefit from outlines, section summaries, or extracted requirements before the full text is included.

00:00:51.774 --> 00:00:53.890
Over-compression is a real risk.

00:00:53.890 --> 00:01:04.933
If a summary removes uncertainty, exceptions, minority opinions, or evidence trails, the model may produce an answer that sounds confident but misses important nuance.

00:01:04.933 --> 00:01:11.413
Compression should preserve the information needed for the task, not merely make the text shorter.

00:01:11.413 --> 00:01:18.819
For high-stakes work, keep links or citations back to the original material so reviewers can verify the summary.

00:01:18.819 --> 00:01:20.538
Staged prompting can help.

00:01:20.538 --> 00:01:23.712
First ask for an outline, inventory, or summary.

00:01:23.712 --> 00:01:27.679
Then ask for a focused analysis using that prepared context.

00:01:27.679 --> 00:01:37.201
For complex workflows, maintain a versioned project summary that includes decisions, open questions, current assumptions, and excluded material.

00:01:37.201 --> 00:01:44.408
This gives the model a compact but useful working memory without forcing every request to include everything.
